    },
    {
      "check": "identifier overlap by UniProt accession",
      "possible": false,
      "how": "the kNN reference files are keyed by UniProt ENTRY NAME, not accession; mapping entry names to accessions needs the UniProt ID-mapping service, i.e. a network query. Only bin/.../all.seq is accession-keyed, and that file feeds the classical-PSORT tables, not the kNN prediction.",
      "coverage": "blocked without a network lookup"
    },
    {
      "check": "overlap against the kNN FEATURE matrix as such",
      "possible": false,
      "how": "data/*.wolff contains only transformed features; it carries no sequence. Overlap can be established only through the matching identifier in data/*.psort, never from the feature vector itself.",
      "coverage": "not a sequence-level check"
    },
    {
      "check": "label agreement between the reference set and the cohort",
      "possible": true,
      "how": "only for proteins matched by exact sequence first; the class vocabularies differ (WoLF 'extr'/'cyto' + dual classes vs the frozen DeepLoc binary labels) and would need an explicit, pre-registered mapping",
      "coverage": "conditional on the exact-sequence match above"
    }
  ],
  "unresolved_limitations": [
    "No provenance or date is recorded in the package for how the reference sets were assembled, so their relationship to the DeepLoc 2.0 cohort cannot be established from the distribution alone.",
    "The reference identifiers are UniProt entry names, which are not stable keys: an entry name can be reassigned between releases, so even a successful name-based match would not prove record identity.",
    "A sequence that is absent from the reference set may still have close homologues in it. Exact-hash overlap is a lower bound on dependence, not a measure of independence.",
    "data/animal.psort has 9 duplicated identifiers and data/animal.wolff carries 5 identifiers with no sequence record, so the two files are not in exact bijection for the animal model."
  ]
